## Brand & Style
The design system focuses on a high-end, academic-meets-tech aesthetic. It prioritizes clarity, cognitive ease, and a sophisticated atmosphere that allows content and data to remain the focal point. By utilizing a "monochromatic premium" style, the system adopts whitespace and grayscale depth to establish hierarchy. The personality is authoritative yet approachable, reflecting the reliability needed for institutional workflows and the innovation of AI integration.

The style blends **Minimalism** with **Modern Corporate** influences, favoring moderate structural alignment, standard breathing room, and a tactile quality achieved through soft shadows rather than vibrant hues.

## Colors
This design system utilizes a strictly neutral palette to convey professional rigor. The primary color is a deep Slate (#0F172A), used for core interactions and primary text to ensure high legibility and a grounded feel. Secondary tones (#64748B) are pulled from the Cool Gray scale to handle supportive information and decorative elements.

Backgrounds transition from pure white for the base canvas to light gray washes (#F8FAFC) for container differentiation. This monochromatic approach relies on varying shades of slate and gray to provide visual feedback and state changes without the need for traditional chromatic accents.

## Typography
Manrope is the sole typeface, chosen for its geometric foundation and modern clarity. The hierarchy is structured to support complex information density common in AI-driven SaaS platforms. 

Headlines utilize tighter tracking and heavier weights to anchor pages, while body copy maintains a generous line height for maximum readability. Labels and captions are set with slightly increased letter spacing and semi-bold weights to ensure they remain distinct from body text even at smaller scales.

## Layout & Spacing
The layout follows a fluid grid model with a base-8 spacing scale (Normal/Level 2) ensuring mathematical harmony across all components. Layouts favor clean whitespace to separate distinct functional areas. Margins are kept at 32px to create a "framed" feel for the content, while gutters are fixed at 24px to ensure enough air between data columns.

## Elevation & Depth
Depth is created through ambient shadows and tonal layers. Surfaces rely on soft, multi-layered shadows with a low-opacity slate tint to suggest lift.

- **Level 0 (Base):** White background.
- **Level 1 (Sub-surface):** Subtle gray washes (#F8FAFC) used for sidebars.
- **Level 2 (Cards):** Elevated white surfaces with a soft shadow.
- **Level 3 (Modals):** Higher lift with a more pronounced shadow.

## Shapes
The shape language is defined by moderate roundedness (Level 2), providing a friendly, modern contrast to the stark grayscale palette. This setting applies to primary containers, cards, and large buttons. Smaller elements like tags or checkboxes scale down proportionally to maintain visual consistency.

## Components
- **Buttons:** Primary buttons are Solid Slate (#0F172A) with white text. Secondary buttons are Outlined. All buttons feature moderate corners and subtle transitions on hover.
- **Input Fields:** Minimal approach with light gray fills (#F1F5F9) and a 1px Slate border on focus.
- **Cards:** The core of the system. Cards feature Level 2 elevation, moderate rounding, and 24px internal padding.
- **Chips/Tags:** Pill-shaped with a light slate background and medium slate text.
- **AI Feedback Indicators:** Small, monochromatic pulse animations or subtle shimmer effects are used during AI processing to maintain the premium feel.